<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>english language Half Yearly</title>
<style>
body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.4; margin: 20px; }
.header { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class='header'>
    <h2>RRB Group of Schools</h2>
    <h3>Half Yearly — english language (Class 5 A)</h3>
</div>
<table width='100%' style='margin-bottom:15px;font-weight:bold;'>
    <tr>
        <td>Time Allowed: 2hrs</td>
        <td align='right'>Maximum Marks: 60</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Teacher: Admin</td>
        <td align='right'>Date: 20/08/2026</td>
    </tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Choose the correct option for each of the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Identify the collective noun in the following sentence: 'A _______ of wolves attacked the flock of sheep.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) herd</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) pack</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) pride</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) flock</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Which of the following words is an Abstract Noun?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Teacher</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Honesty</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) River</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Book</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Choose the correct reflexive pronoun to complete the sentence: 'She hurt _______ while playing in the garden.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) her</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) hers</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) herself</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) she</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> Select the correct superlative degree of the adjective: 'Mount Everest is the _______ peak in the world.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) high</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) higher</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) highest</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) most high</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Identify the adverb of frequency in the sentence: 'He usually goes to the library on Saturdays.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) goes</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) library</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) usually</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Saturdays</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> Identify the type of sentence: 'What a beautiful painting this is!'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Declarative Sentence</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Imperative Sentence</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Interrogative Sentence</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Exclamatory Sentence</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> Choose the correct preposition: 'The energetic cat jumped _______ the wall.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) over</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) in</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) at</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) under</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Which of the following words is a synonym of 'Ancient'?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Modern</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Old</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Fresh</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Young</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Choose the correct conjunction: 'We stayed indoors _______ it was raining heavily.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) but</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) because</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) or</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) although</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> Select the correct article: 'He wants to become _______ honest officer when he grows up.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) a</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) an</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) the</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) no article</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section B: Fill in the Blanks</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Fill in the blanks with the appropriate words as instructed.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> A _______ of bees buzzed continuously around the garden flowers.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> The children were excited _______ they were going to visit the zoo.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Riya has been living in Kolkata _______ 2018.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> Neither Rahul nor his friends _______ present in the class yesterday.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> She speaks English _______ (fluent). [Use the correct form of Adverb]</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> _______ sun shines brightly in the summer sky.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> The mother divided the chocolate slice _______ the two brothers.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> The frightened puppy hid _______ the bed during the thunderstorm.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Cruelty is the opposite of _______ (kind). [Form an Abstract Noun]</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> She _______ (finish) her homework before going out to play. [Use Past Perfect Tense]</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section C: True / False</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: State whether the following statements are True or False.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> An imperative sentence always expresses a strong feeling or emotion.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Abstract nouns refer to ideas, qualities, or conditions that cannot be touched.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> The word 'quickly' acts as an adjective in the sentence: 'He ran quickly.'</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> The word 'The' is known as an indefinite article.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Transitive verbs require an object to complete their meaning.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> Prepositions show the relationship between a noun or pronoun and other words in a sentence.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> The simple past tense form of the verb 'teach' is 'teached'.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Conjunctions are joining words used to connect words, phrases, or clauses.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> The superlative degree of 'good' is 'better'.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> The word 'mine' is an example of a possessive pronoun.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section D: Very Short Answer</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions as directed.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Rewrite the sentence changing the verb into Simple Past Tense: 'She writes a letter to her grandmother.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Identify the Subject and Predicate in the following sentence: 'The brave fireman rescued the little boy from the house.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Change the following assertive sentence into an Interrogative sentence: 'Rohan can play the guitar very well.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> Underline the adjective and state its type: 'These five books belong to my sister.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Punctuate the following sentence using appropriate punctuation marks and capital letters: 'where are you going riya asked sumit'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> Form Abstract Nouns from the following words:
(a) Brave
(b) Wise</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> Underline the verb in the sentence and state whether it is Transitive or Intransitive: 'The birds sang sweetly in the morning.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Combine the sentences using a suitable conjunction: 'It was very cold. We did not go swimming.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Fill in the blank with a suitable Possessive Pronoun: 'This blue bicycle belongs to me. It is _______.'</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> Change the following active voice sentence into passive voice: 'The chef cooked a delicious meal.'</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section E: Long Answer</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following descriptive questions in detail.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Write a well-structured paragraph in about 80–100 words on ANY ONE of the following topics:
(a) My Favorite Hobby
(b) A Day I Spent with My Grandparents</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow:

One sunny afternoon, a young boy named Aryan was walking home from school. As he passed by the old banyan tree near the village square, he heard a faint chirping sound. Looking closely among the bushes, he found a tiny injured bird. Its wing was hurt and it could not fly. Aryan gently picked up the bird, wrapped it in his soft handkerchief, and brought it home. His mother helped him clean the bird's wound and put some balm on it. They kept the bird in a comfortable shoe box lined with cotton. For three days, Aryan fed the bird water and grain. On the fourth morning, the bird fluttered its wings and flew happily out of the open window. Aryan felt joyful seeing the little bird fly again.</div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>Where did Aryan find the injured bird?</li><li>How did Aryan carry the bird safely to his home?</li><li>How did Aryan's mother help in treating the bird?</li><li>For how many days did Aryan take care of the bird before it flew away?</li><li>Find a word from the passage that means 'delighted' or 'very happy'.</li></ol>
</body>
</html>